    "done_when": "Argue both sides of a proposed pivot for nova's forward solve: stop carrying accuracy on polynomial order, cut-cell geometry and X-point order, and instead raise the plasma cell count (start near 2,000 cells and go upward on the H200), and judge whether the argument is grounded. Done when the report holds: (1) the strongest case for the pivot, each point tied to a measurement or source (for example compile cost measured flat in cell count and dominated by the point jet fourth derivative, GPU suitability for many cells, the size of the machinery built); (2) the strongest case against, each point tied to a measurement or source (for example quantities whose measured order is below one, such as the half-order saddle membership, which refinement improves only slowly; boundary and limiter-contact errors that are geometric; dense coupling of size cells squared; any acceptance clause independent of resolution); (3) for each acceptance clause of the converged-forward-solve section 6 table, whether refinement, higher order, or both is the cheaper route, with the reasoning and the evidence; (4) a recommended direction with the two or three measurements that would confirm or refute it fastest, and what in the current plans to stop, keep or redirect. Write this independently: do not read reports other workers produce for the same question. Work read-only: read plans under docs/plans, research under docs/research, evidence fragments under docs/evidence, receipts and figures under docs/figures and the GPFS evidence root, run directories under /home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/runs that belong to project nova, the committed ledger docs/state/nova, and the source under nova/ and tests/. Every number you report carries its source (file path and anchor, or run id and log), and every claim that is an inference rather than a measurement says so. Deliver the report as one markdown file at the assigned write path, with the required tables, and write the manifest with status complete, blocked or failed, which you set yourself.",
